    {"id": 5, "claim": "While 'becoming suspect' is a temporary state of evaluation, it is not the formal constructive outcome of the scientific process.", "evidence": "Comparison of 'suspect' (a status) vs 'modified' (an action/outcome) in the context of scientific rigor; 'suspect' is passive, while 'modified' is the active resolution.", "weight": 0.05, "depends_on": [4]}
